* 18 Oct 26 dm  New (terminal 140 by 42, phase 2): the one place that says how big the window is.  $sl_need (the refusal)
*               and $sl_guard (the cursor lock) ask it.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_window(w, h)
*
*     w h   the size of the window a program can draw on, in cells: the display SD has (@CRTWIDE by @CRTHIGH, which the kernel
*           keeps to the tty's own size and which TERM w,h sets by hand), or the tty's own size if that is smaller (TERM 200,60
*           typed in an 80 by 24 window does not make the window bigger).  Read afresh each time: a resize changes it.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_window(w, h)
$catalog $sl_window

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   w = @crtwide + 0
   h = @crthigh + 0
   ws = kernel(K$WINSIZE, '')
   if ws # '' then
      if ws<1> + 0 < w then w = ws<1> + 0
      if ws<2> + 0 < h then h = ws<2> + 0
   end

   return
end

* END-CODE
